PATCH 340: the a904->e200->e21c LOS-probe path -- pass HOST pointers to the e21c LOS-query builder
(patch 334, host-pointer convention) from this second caller path.  a904 (already reconstructed by
patch 269, object di in param_1) forwarded its candidate cell entry and its object as NEAR OFFSETS to
e200, and e200 typed its object param `undefined2` (truncating it); e21c then dereferenced [cand+4]/
[obj+4] at the near-address -> SIGSEGV (fault ~0xc15b, chain c0e5->7c1d->a904->e200->e21c).  The crash
MIGRATED here once patch 339 cleared the ab7f twin.

ROOT CAUSE (asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin @ 0xa904/0xe200; DS=SS=DGROUP=0x1c00):
a904 keeps bx=candidate (near offset word[DGROUP:(...+0x6d3c)]) and di=object live and falls into e21c
via e200.  e21c (patch 334) dereferences its candidate/object params as HOST pointers.  Patch 269's a904
passed them as raw near offsets (`(int*)ent`, `(undefined2)di`), and e200's undefined2 object param
truncated further.

THE FIX (two spots): a904's e200 call rebases both the candidate (dg+ent) and the object (dg+di) to
host pointers; e200's param_2 (object) widened undefined2 -> int so the 32-bit host pointer passes intact.
Mission-cascade only -> behaviour-neutral for the 24 verify flows.
